The doz program is built with third-party software. Most of it is licensed under the Apache License,
Version 2.0, and several of those components carry NOTICE files whose attribution notices must be
reproduced with any distribution of a binary that contains them. Every release of doz therefore ships,
in libexec/doz/licences/, the complete licence text and the verbatim NOTICE file of each component, taken
from the exact sources the release was built from (THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt, written by
Scripts/third-party-licences.sh). The components and their licences are listed in LICENCES.md.

Among the attributions those NOTICE files require:

- SwiftNIO, SwiftNIO SSL, SwiftNIO HTTP/2, SwiftNIO Extras, AsyncHTTPClient, Swift Crypto, Swift
  Certificates, Swift ASN.1, Swift Log, Swift HTTP Types, Swift Service Context, Swift Service Lifecycle,
  Swift Configuration and gRPC Swift — Copyright Apple Inc. and the SwiftNIO / Swift Server / gRPC
  project authors (Apache-2.0).
- SwiftNIO SSL contains code from BoringSSL (a combination of the ISC and OpenSSL licences);
  Swift Crypto (its _CryptoExtras, through Swift Certificates) contains BoringSSL as well.
- SwiftNIO contains NodeJS's llhttp (MIT), "sha1.c"/"sha1.h" from FreeBSD (Copyright (C) 1995-1998
  WIDE Project, BSD) and "cpp_magic.h" from uSHET (MIT), and is heavily influenced by Netty (Apache-2.0).
- Swift Certificates contains code derived from musl libc (MIT).
- Docker's .dockerignore semantics (Sources/DozerKit/DockerIgnore.swift and dozview's match/dozmatch.c) are ports of
  moby/patternmatcher v0.6.1 — "Docker. Copyright 2012-2017 Docker, Inc. This product includes software developed
  at Docker, Inc. (https://www.docker.com)." (Apache-2.0) — and of tonistiigi/fsutil (MIT, Copyright 2017 Tõnis Tiigi).
- dozview's regular-expression engine (match/dozre.c) and the path functions beside it are ports of Go's
  regexp/syntax, path and path/filepath — Copyright 2009 The Go Authors (BSD-3-Clause).
- BoringSSL's licence texts (OpenSSL, SSLeay, ISC, MIT for third_party/fiat), LibYAML's (MIT, Copyright (c) 2006 Kirill
  Simonov) and the above are in Licences/, fetched at the exact revisions Licences/SOURCES.md names.

The guest programs doz copies into each sandbox (deckhold, doznet, dozview) statically link musl libc
(MIT); deckhold also links libghostty-vt from Ghostty (MIT) and its bundled simdutf, Highway and LLVM
libc++ (see LICENCES.md). The dashboard serves ghostty-web (MIT) and Lucide icons (ISC) to your browser.
